Z||000000||Patrick's Dad||10-30-2001||10:20 PM||||After all, it wasn't my fault it's stuck....<P>So, I'm working on taking my 2.8 out of the Formula, and I figure that now (not really now, but then, when I was working on it) would be a good time to remove the slave cylinder and the cables from the Muncie. There's a bracket that has a bolt that (to me) was impossible to get to from the top, so's I go at it from the bottom. I stick my socket wrench in there and start cranking. Everything's fine until I get a little resistance. I wrench the bolt back a bit. Everything's fine, so I click into "remove" again, and start wrenching. It gets tough again, so I get tougher. Well I got so tough that I failed to see that my wrench was backing into a frame member (possibly part of the cradle), and is now stuck until I remove the assembly and disassemble it....<P>I wonder if Sears will replace the ratchet. It certainly didn't perform to my expectations....||||reg||12
